<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Radon in Saskatoon is less common than in Regina or Winnipeg, but it isn't rare. Of the Saskatoon homes tested in the 2024 Cross-Canada Survey, 17.8% were at or above 200 Bq/m3 (becquerels per cubic metre, the Canadian unit) and another 44.3% landed between 100 and 199. Those are unweighted figures from homes that chose to test, so read them as a rough picture, not a census.</p><p>Radon is a colourless, odourless gas that seeps up from the ground and collects in basements. Health Canada says it's the number one cause of lung cancer in non-smokers, and that's the last time we'll say it this loudly. Prairie Radon Co connects homeowners in Saskatoon, Warman, Martensville and the acreages around the city with independent radon professionals. Our advice on the first step costs you nothing: <a href="/radon-testing/">run a long-term test</a> before anyone quotes you a system.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Saskatoon</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Saskatoon Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Long-term radon testing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Health Canada acts on a test of at least 91 days in the heating season, placed in your lowest lived-in level. Kits from the lung associations' HomeRadonTest.ca run about $70 before tax and are analysed at the Saskatchewan Research Council lab.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Radon mitigation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If a long-term result comes back over 200 Bq/m3, a certified mitigation professional can install sub-slab depressurization: a pipe through the basement slab, a fan, and a discharge outside. No Saskatoon installer publishes a price, so the professional quotes your house.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Radon and home sales</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Buying or selling in Saskatoon and radon has come up in the conditions? A C-NRPP measurement professional can explain what a short timeline can and can't tell you, while your realtor or lawyer handles the paperwork.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Fan and system checks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A noisy fan, a dead fan or a manometer that reads wrong all mean the system needs a look. Health Canada's 2014 national figure for a fan replacement is $200 to $300; a professional will quote the actual job.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
